  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes:\n• Bunifu TextBox: Fixed duplicate event triggers for the `TextChanged` event.\n• Bunifu Button 2: Fixed color inconsistencies during state transitions.\n• Bunifu Transitions: Can now be safely disposed at runtime.\n\nUpdates:\nThis release partially supports .Net 9 and is currently on experimental preview. If you're upgrading to .Net 9, we would advise you to backup your existing project before upgrading. If you face any long-standing issues, kindly downgrade to .Net 8 as we work on fully supporting .Net 9 in the upcoming releases. Thank you.\n\nExtras: Breaking Changes - Licensing:\nIn this release, we have revamped our licensing architecture from the old .Net Framework standard. Therefore, if you happen to receive errors relating to the \"Licenses.licx\" file, please go ahead and delete the file then clean and rebuild your project. For more info, please visit https://docs2.bunifuframework.com/docs/getting-started/installation-net5plus\n\nExtras: Migration Notes:\nIf you're upgrading from a project using the deprecated version 1.5.3, please install 'Bunifu.UI.WinForms.1.5.3' (version 2.0.0) via NuGet for backward compatibility with newer releases of Bunifu.UI.WinForms. Also, if you're building a VB.NET project and after installation receive ambiguous namespace errors (e.g. BunifuTextBox has an ambiguous namespace...), please install 'Bunifu.UI.WinForms.Deprecated' (version 2.0.0) via NuGet then rebuild your project. In case of any further upgrade issues, feel free to contact us via our bottom-right chat section at https://bunifuframework.com/.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
